  "schema_semantic_checks": [
    "Reject duplicate JSON object keys and NaN/infinity before schema validation.",
    "Span turn_id must equal binding.turn_id; 0<=start<end<=len(original_text); evidence must actually support the labelled role. Offset equality alone is not semantic support.",
    "Binding hashes/revision/turn must exactly equal current input; wrapper controls model_id and bindings.",
    "Unique clause IDs, unique component names per clause, finite scores and valid calibration/model references.",
    "Every target index and offer/readback/supersedes reference exists in the legitimate input state, with current permissible scope.",
    "No positive asserted complete value may be inferred from a negated/conditional/quoted/questioned span or unfinished token. Source normalization remains independent.",
    "status=proposed requires no unresolved authority-relevant field in the proposed scope; otherwise partial/abstain. Partial is never joint permission.",
    "Accept decision requires independently qualified trained/calibrated head and frozen thresholds; non-null score alone cannot set decision=accept.",
    "Empty input yields primary=null and abstain; no invalid zero-length evidence span. Unknown schema, budget overflow and runtime exception return a bound neutral abstain wrapper.",
    "No current raw text binding in platform means no unqualified promotion from extracted_copy to trusted_turn."
  ],
